1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,802
Payment Desk checks supplier invoices before they are paid. AI investigates. Code decides.

2
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:11,388
This is the scripted demo. The Mozaik runtime, five agents, shared state, tools and controls run for real; the model's answers are predefined.

3
00:00:11,388 --> 00:00:15,453
Four synthetic invoices, one at a time, through the real workflow.

4
00:00:15,453 --> 00:00:20,736
Scenario 1: a valid invoice. The Extractor reads it; then the Validator and the Auditor start from the same event and run in parallel.

5
00:00:20,736 --> 00:00:25,858
Every control passes and the amount is under the limit: approved, with a sandbox draft. No money moves.

6
00:00:25,858 --> 00:00:31,364
Scenario 2: the invoice asks for payment to a new bank account. It is not the account on file for this vendor.

7
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:38,623
Blocked by a control in code. The Policy agent cannot loosen it, and there is no approve button.

8
00:00:38,623 --> 00:00:44,527
Scenario 3: a two-page PDF. The cover text asks for 1,980.00; the invoice total says 1,890.00.

9
00:00:44,527 --> 00:00:56,440
Each amount opens the original PDF page, with the cited line marked where the parser found it.

10
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:04,100
The Auditor read the document without seeing the first reading and reported both amounts. Code recorded the disagreement as a challenge.

11
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:10,342
Which amount is owed? The invoice cannot say. A confirmation on record as unverified is refused.

12
00:01:10,342 --> 00:01:21,161
A verified vendor confirmation for this invoice and this amount settles it. Only then may a person approve.

13
00:01:21,161 --> 00:01:29,441
Stress lab: twelve scenarios, each declaring its outcome before it runs. Every execution gets its own process and its own Mozaik runtime.

14
00:01:29,441 --> 00:01:38,690
A controlled fault-injection test, not a model benchmark: nine deliberate agent errors, each run with one agent and with five.

15
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:47,395
Code stops seven of them either way. One, a line item quoted correctly as the total where code does not know the label, is approved by a single agent and stopped only by the independent second reading.

16
00:01:47,395 --> 00:01:52,686
And one gets through: both readers make the same mistake. The test reports it as not caught, a limit declared in advance.

17
00:01:52,686 --> 00:02:00,236
A recording, not live: a real model on a laptop (qwen2.5:7b, 27 November) ran the four scenarios on this code. All four ended as expected.

18
00:02:00,236 --> 00:02:05,923
Here the Auditor found both amounts on its own. Every loop names the model that ran it. Earlier runs that went worse are kept beside it.

19
00:02:05,923 --> 00:02:13,013
Every agent loop is recorded by the runtime: when it started, what triggered it, when it finished. The Validator and the Auditor overlap.

20
00:02:13,013 --> 00:02:19,364
Every payment has one decision record, assembled by code from the case: sources, agent findings, controls, enforcement, review history.

21
00:02:19,364 --> 00:02:25,800
AI investigates. Code decides.   github.com/lukovic75/payment-desk   ·   npm ci && npm run demo

